Alessi, 38 years old,

258
00:17:12,673 --> 00:17:14,908
single, and an unfortunate projectile,

259
00:17:15,273 --> 00:17:16,332
out of commission!

260
00:17:32,493 --> 00:17:34,193
Was all of that a dream?

261
00:17:40,953 --> 00:17:47,170
This earring belongs to that boy so
it really did happen I don't know why

262
00:17:47,253 --> 00:17:52,810
but for some reason I couldn't move
my body that's right I may not have

263
00:17:52,893 --> 00:17:57,850
been able to move but I remember
everything That sweet little boy devoted

264
00:17:57,933 --> 00:18:02,573
himself to protecting me and risked his
life by fighting against a grown man.

265
00:18:02,953 --> 00:18:05,193
He has such a brave and heroic heart.

266
00:18:05,593 --> 00:18:07,173
Oh, where did that boy go?

267
00:18:07,933 --> 00:18:08,763
Where?

268
00:18:08,933 --> 00:18:11,168
Where did my little knight run off to?

269
00:18:12,353 --> 00:18:13,533
Where did you go?

270
00:18:13,793 --> 00:18:14,773
Where are you?

271
00:18:17,813 --> 00:18:20,433
I've never met such an
amazing woman before.

272
00:18:20,693 --> 00:18:21,753
So kind.

273
00:18:22,033 --> 00:18:22,893
So genuine.

274
00:18:23,893 --> 00:18:27,658
That was a close one, but thankfully
I'm back to my normal self.

275
00:18:28,113 --> 00:18:29,853
I wonder if she's okay.

276
00:18:38,213 --> 00:18:39,370
I hate to bother you,

277
00:18:39,453 --> 00:18:41,510
but you didn't happen
to see a sweet little

278
00:18:41,593 --> 00:18:43,310
boy leave my house in
something of a hurry,

279
00:18:43,393 --> 00:18:44,223
did you?

280
00:18:44,873 --> 00:18:46,050
He has silver hair.

281
00:18:46,133 --> 00:18:49,015
Come to think of it, it
looks exactly like yours.

282
00:18:57,693 --> 00:19:00,987
Pardon me for asking, but
have the two of us met before?

283
00:19:05,993 --> 00:19:08,111
No, I didn't see a kid come through.

284
00:19:08,373 --> 00:19:09,902
Sorry I couldn't help you.

285
00:19:10,393 --> 00:19:11,393
Let's go, Jotaro.

286
00:19:14,133 --> 00:19:15,733
Come on, hurry up!

287
00:19:17,193 --> 00:19:18,053
Please, wait!

288
00:19:18,833 --> 00:19:20,090
Could you be...

289
00:19:20,173 --> 00:19:21,820
that earring you're wearing?

290
00:19:23,613 --> 00:19:25,753
The two of us have never met before.

291
00:19:26,413 --> 00:19:27,613
It's not possible.

292
00:19:28,173 --> 00:19:29,938
My friend and I are travelers.

293
00:19:30,693 --> 00:19:34,458
So, if you'll excuse us, there's
another town we need to get to.

294
00:19:34,873 --> 00:19:36,093
We'll be going now.

295
00:19:41,433 --> 00:19:43,093
It was only a dream.

296
00:19:43,813 --> 00:19:44,693
Too bad.

297
00:19:51,973 --> 00:19:54,233
Not a single word from you, Jotaro.

298
00:19:54,533 --> 00:19:55,945
I don't want to hear it.

299
00:20:02,433 --> 00:20:03,263
No!

300
00:20:03,613 --> 00:20:05,293
Jotaro and Polnareff!

301
00:20:05,753 --> 00:20:08,390
Where in the world have
you two slackers been?

302
00:20:08,473 --> 00:20:09,453
Ah, Mr.

303
00:20:09,593 --> 00:20:10,773
Joestar and Avdol.

304
00:20:11,693 --> 00:20:15,650
How many times have I told the two of
you not to go wandering off on your own?

305
00:20:15,733 --> 00:20:17,350
Oh, you're in a position to talk.

306
00:20:17,433 --> 00:20:19,609
You're the ones who just disappeared.

307
00:20:20,113 --> 00:20:20,943
Now, now.

308
00:20:21,173 --> 00:20:23,890
Why don't we focus on
getting something to eat?

309
00:20:23,973 --> 00:20:25,233
Huh? Hey, Iggy!

310
00:20:25,393 --> 00:20:27,864
Where the hell have you been all day long?

311
00:20:39,913 --> 00:20:41,390
Can I take that for you?

312
00:20:41,473 --> 00:20:45,930
Yeah, thanks a million!

313
00:20:46,013 --> 00:20:51,010
It's about time we're finally
getting a bit of relief.

314
00:20:51,093 --> 00:20:54,890
It was quite the late breakfast but
I suppose it couldn't be helped.

315
00:20:54,973 --> 00:20:58,250
Yeah, since we've almost made it to Cairo,

316
00:20:58,333 --> 00:21:01,290
I think it's time we figured
out where Dio is hiding out.

317
00:21:01,373 --> 00:21:04,810
Oh, we're doing this.

318
00:21:04,893 --> 00:21:06,050
Will it appear?

319
00:21:06,133 --> 00:21:07,110
I'm not sure.

320
00:21:07,193 --> 00:21:10,410
But given that we're so close, the
results should be more precise.

321
00:21:10,493 --> 00:21:11,590
All right.

322
00:21:11,673 --> 00:21:12,773
Here we go!

323
00:21:20,173 --> 00:21:21,373
Excuse me, sir.

324
00:21:21,573 --> 00:21:22,970
Is there a problem over here?

325
00:21:23,053 --> 00:21:24,112
Everything's fine.

326
00:21:24,293 --> 00:21:25,646
Mind your own business.

327
00:21:25,833 --> 00:21:26,793
Yes, sir.

328
00:21:30,533 --> 00:21:32,653
Old man, tell us.

329
00:21:32,793 --> 00:21:33,673
What is it?

330
00:21:33,993 --> 00:21:35,353
Just a little longer.

331
00:21:35,873 --> 00:21:37,353
I see something.

332
00:21:37,853 --> 00:21:39,453
It's getting clearer.

333
00:21:41,673 --> 00:21:42,913
Take a good look!

334
00:21:45,533 --> 00:21:48,592
There you have it, gentlemen,
our final destination!

335
00:22:17,773 --> 00:22:19,093
Thank you.

336
00:22:48,113 --> 00:22:48,943
Thank you.

337
00:23:28,213 --> 00:23:29,930
You're the one who fell for the scam.

338
00:23:30,013 --> 00:23:31,850
I've had just about enough of your games.

339
00:23:31,933 --> 00:23:33,730
Gambling is just like relationships.

340
00:23:33,813 --> 00:23:35,190
The one who cries loses.

341
00:23:35,273 --> 00:23:37,910
If he does anything that
seems suspicious, you can go.

342
00:23:37,993 --> 00:23:42,493
If you're scared, exactly right,
I'm going to bet my soul. Good.
